WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.925
You plot a DR.

2
00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:03.900
You take a fix.

3
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.750
They don’t agree.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.900
That isn’t a mistake.

5
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.900
It’s information.

6
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.775
The gap between them is the current, plus any wind and steering error, and you can measure it.

7
00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:17.850
Look at the diagram.

8
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.650
Two words.

9
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.000
Set is the direction the current is pushing you.

10
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.150
Drift is its speed.

11
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:31.275
To find the set, measure the direction from your DR position to your fix, at the same time.

12
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:37.650
To find the drift, measure the distance between them, and divide by the hours since your last fix.

13
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.150
Now the trap, and it catches nearly everyone once.

14
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.350
Which way do you measure?

15
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.975
From the DR, toward the fix.

16
00:00:47.225 --> 00:00:50.400
From where you thought you were, to where you really are.

17
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:56.225
Measure it backward, and you get the reciprocal, exactly one hundred eighty degrees wrong.

18
00:00:56.475 --> 00:01:00.400
And that wrong answer is almost always one of the choices.
